# TEngine Framework Architecture

## Overview

This project uses **TEngine Framework** - a modular Unity framework with hot-update support. The architecture follows a layered approach with clear separation between framework core, main domain, and hot-update domain.

## Architecture Layers

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   Hot Update Domain (HotFix/)          │
│   - GameLogic/ (Game Logic)            │
│   - GameProto/ (Config Protocol)       │
│   - Access via GameModule              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   Main Domain (GameScripts/)            │
│   - GameEntry.cs (Entry Point)         │
│   - Procedure/ (FSM State Machine)      │
│   - Access via ModuleSystem             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│   Framework Core (TEngine/)            │
│   - Module System                       │
│   - ResourceModule (YooAsset)          │
│   - ProcedureModule (FSM)               │
│   - AudioModule                         │
│   - LocalizationModule                  │
│   - ObjectPoolModule                    │
│   - TimerModule                         │
│   - SceneModule                         │
│   - DebuggerModule                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Module System

### Framework Modules (Main Domain)

Access framework modules via `ModuleSystem.GetModule<T>()`:

```csharp
// In main domain (Procedure, GameEntry, etc.)
var resourceModule = ModuleSystem.GetModule<IResourceModule>();
var audioModule = ModuleSystem.GetModule<IAudioModule>();
var procedureModule = ModuleSystem.GetModule<IProcedureModule>();
```

### Game Modules (Hot Update Domain)

Access game modules via `GameModule` static class:

```csharp
// In hot update domain (GameLogic)
GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<LoginUI>();
GameModule.Resource.LoadAssetAsync<GameObject>("Player");
GameModule.Audio.PlaySound("Click");
GameModule.Scene.LoadSceneAsync("Battle");
```

## Procedure System (FSM)

The Procedure system manages game state flow using a Finite State Machine pattern.

### Procedure Flow

```
Launch → Splash → InitPackage → InitResources → LoadAssembly → StartGame
```

### Creating a Procedure

```csharp
namespace Procedure
{
    public class ProcedureLaunch : ProcedureBase
    {
        public override bool UseNativeDialog => true;
        
        private IAudioModule _audioModule;

        protected override void OnInit(IFsm<IProcedureModule> procedureOwner)
        {
            _audioModule = ModuleSystem.GetModule<IAudioModule>();
            base.OnInit(procedureOwner);
        }

        protected override void OnEnter(IFsm<IProcedureModule> procedureOwner)
        {
            base.OnEnter(procedureOwner);
            // Initialization logic
        }

        protected override void OnUpdate(IFsm<IProcedureModule> procedureOwner, float elapseSeconds, float realElapseSeconds)
        {
            base.OnUpdate(procedureOwner, elapseSeconds, realElapseSeconds);
            
            // State transition
            ChangeState<ProcedureSplash>(procedureOwner);
        }

        protected override void OnExit(IFsm<IProcedureModule> procedureOwner, bool isShutdown)
        {
            base.OnExit(procedureOwner, isShutdown);
            // Cleanup logic
        }
    }
}
```

## Hot Update Architecture (HybridCLR)

### Domain Separation

- **Main Domain**: `GameScripts/` - Core framework and procedures
- **Hot Update Domain**: `HotFix/GameLogic/` - Game logic that can be hot-updated

### Entry Point

```csharp
// Hot update entry point (called after assembly loaded)
public partial class GameApp
{
    public static void Entrance(object[] objects)
    {
        GameEventHelper.Init();
        _hotfixAssembly = (List<Assembly>)objects[0];
        StartGameLogic();
    }
    
    private static void StartGameLogic()
    {
        // Start game logic
        GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<BattleMainUI>();
    }
}
```

### Hot Update Code Placement

- ✅ **DO**: Place hot update code in `HotFix/GameLogic/` assembly
- ✅ **DO**: Access framework via `GameModule` static class
- ❌ **DON'T**: Put hot update code in main domain
- ❌ **DON'T**: Access modules directly - use `GameModule`

## Resource Management (YooAsset)

### Loading Resources

```csharp
// Async loading (preferred)
var handle = await GameModule.Resource.LoadAssetAsync<GameObject>("Player");
GameObject player = handle.AssetObject as GameObject;

// Sync loading (use sparingly)
var handle = GameModule.Resource.LoadAssetSync<GameObject>("Player");
```

### Resource Rules

- ✅ **DO**: Use YooAsset for all resource loading
- ✅ **DO**: Use `LoadAssetAsync` for async loading (preferred)
- ✅ **DO**: Use `LoadAssetSync` for sync loading (use sparingly)
- ❌ **DON'T**: Use `Resources.Load()` - forbidden
- ❌ **DON'T**: Forget to release handles (framework manages automatically)

**Note:** `LoadGameObject` is used internally by UIModule for UI prefabs. For general resource loading, use `LoadAssetAsync` or `LoadAssetSync`.

## Event System

### GameEvent Pattern

TEngine supports two event patterns. Use `GameEvent.AddEventListener` and `GameEvent.Send` for general game events.

```csharp
// Define event constants
public static class ActorEventDefine
{
    public const int PlayerDead = 1001;
    public const int EnemyDead = 1002;
    public const int ScoreChange = 1003;
    public const int GameOver = 1004;
}

// Register event listener
GameEvent.AddEventListener<Vector3, Quaternion>(ActorEventDefine.PlayerDead, OnPlayerDead);

// Send event
GameEvent.Send(ActorEventDefine.PlayerDead, position, rotation);

// Remove event listener
GameEvent.RemoveEventListener<Vector3, Quaternion>(ActorEventDefine.PlayerDead, OnPlayerDead);

// Event handler
private void OnPlayerDead(Vector3 position, Quaternion rotation)
{
    // Handle player death
}
```

### Event Interface Pattern (Alternative - for UI)

```csharp
// Define event interface
public interface ILoginUI : IEvent
{
    void ShowLoginUI();
}

// Implement in UI class
public class LoginUI : UIWindow, ILoginUI
{
    public void ShowLoginUI()
    {
        GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<LoginUI>();
    }
}

// Access event
GameEvent.Get<ILoginUI>().ShowLoginUI();
```

## Best Practices

### Module Access

- **Main Domain**: Use `ModuleSystem.GetModule<T>()`
- **Hot Update Domain**: Use `GameModule.X` static properties

### State Management

- Use **Procedure** system for game state flow
- Don't bypass Procedure system for state management

### Hot Update

- Keep hot update code in `HotFix/GameLogic/` assembly
- Access framework via `GameModule` only
- Test hot update flow: Launch → LoadAssembly → GameApp.Entrance() → StartGameLogic()

### Resource Loading

- Always use YooAsset (never Resources.Load)
- Prefer async loading
- Framework manages resource references automatically
